{# Per-request context. Kept apart from system_prompt.j2 so retrieving new
   memories, portrait or skills never invalidates the cached instruction prefix. #}
{{ portrait_section(user_portrait) }}

{% if persistent_memories %}
## User Context (from memory)
These are always-loaded facts about the user. Reference them naturally.
{% for memory in persistent_memories %}
- {{ memory | memory_record }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% if relevant_memories %}
## Relevant Memories
These memories may be relevant to the current conversation. Use them for context but don't explicitly cite them unless the user asks.
{% for memory in relevant_memories %}
- {{ memory | memory_record }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% if daily_memories %}
## Daily Memories (按天的记忆记录)
Each entry summarizes what the user did on that day. Use them for continuity; when the user asks about a specific day (e.g. "8月9日我们做了什么"), answer from these records.
{% for memory in daily_memories %}
### {{ memory.date.isoformat() }}
{{ memory.content }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% if relevant_skills %}
## Relevant Experience
You have learned methodologies for the following tasks. Use `view_skill` to read
full details and auto-deploy files to the sandbox.
{% for skill in relevant_skills %}
### {{ skill.name }} (ID: {{ skill.id }}, version: {{ skill.version }})
{{ skill.description }}
Verification: {{ (skill.verification | default({}, true)).get('status', 'unverified') }}
{% if skill.files %}
Files:
{% for f in skill.files %}
  - `{{ f.path }}` ({{ f.type }}){% if f.description %}: {{ f.description }}{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% if child_agents %}
## Available Child Agents
You can delegate specialized tasks to the following child agents using the `delegate_task` tool:
{% for child in child_agents %}
- **{{ child.name }}** (ID: `{{ child.id }}`): {{ child.description or "Specialized sub-agent" }}
{% endfor %}

**Delegation guidelines**:
- Use delegation when a task matches a child agent's specialization
- Provide clear task descriptions with sufficient context for independent execution
- Child agents share your sandbox environment and can access files you've created
- You can delegate multiple tasks in parallel by calling `delegate_task` multiple times
{% endif %}
